//! Simplified <-> Traditional Chinese conversion (`text.simplify`, `text.traditional`).
//!
//! The character tables come from the public Unicode Unihan database (Unicode 18.0.0,
//! under the Unicode Terms of Use):
//! `kSimplifiedVariant` from `Unihan_Variants.txt`, plus the
//! project's own 356-pair table, whose deliberate choices (面 -> 面, 发 -> 發, 后 -> 後) win.
//! No external library, no bundled data file: the tables are `const` pairs of strings where
//! matching positions give the two forms.
//!
//! Some characters have more than one traditional form and the right one depends on the word:
//! 干 (干/乾/幹), 复 (复/複/復), 制 (制/製), 里 (里/裡), 表 (表/錶), 松 (松/鬆). Mapping them
//! unconditionally produces wrong characters - 见面 -> 見麵, 干净 -> 幹淨, 制度 -> 製度 - so
//! they are left alone and `PHRASES` carries the words that need the other form. The phrase
//! table is applied in both directions, so traditional -> simplified needs no second list.
//!
//! Scope: a character-and-phrase table, not OpenCC. Regional variants (软件 -> 軟體 in Taiwan)
//! and word-segmentation-sensitive cases need a word segmenter and a phrase database, out of
//! scope here.

